{"id": 22, "ts": 1780642786.8317053, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fB demonstrates solid stress resilience and technical aptitude, the reports of grumpiness and uncooperativeness raise real doubts about crew cooperation on long\u2011haul flights.\u202fCandidate\u202fD, although strong on concentration and problem\u2011solving, is described as arrogant with weak leadership, which could undermine cockpit harmony.\u202fCandidate\u202fA, despite impressive anticipatory skills and leadership potential, is noted as \u201ccan be unorganized\u201d and \u201cnot good at taking criticism,\u201d both red flags for operational reliability and feedback orientation.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC is 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, and makes correct decisions quickly\u2014directly addressing reliability, crew cooperation, and decision quality.\u202fHis communication challenges and egocentric style are concerning, but they appear less likely to jeopardize safety than the reliability and teamwork deficits seen in the other candidates.\u202fTherefore, I continue to provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
